mission "blabla" {
    statement "Small coding models drift from the goal and claim done too early. BlaBla catches that: a human or a strong model writes the project's intent once, as executable contracts and queryable memory, and cheap models do bounded work that BlaBla checks against it. Strong models and people are then spent on the hard calls, not on watching simple work."
    non_goals [
        "Replace strong models. Product thinking, architecture, planning, pushback and hard integration are where a strong model earns its cost; BlaBla keeps that reasoning from being spent again on work a bounded worker can do.",
        "Become a general-purpose language, an agent orchestrator, a BDD framework or a theorem prover. One current contract language and API, with no versioned schemas, migrations or compatibility branches.",
        "Let project memory decide completion. Mission, System, Process and Knowledge never count toward OVERALL, and a project without them is not incomplete.",
        "Claim enforcement BlaBla does not have. A policy is called enforced only while a trusted mechanism actually enforces it.",
        "Prove anything. A behavior campaign is a bounded search and structure reads only what a provider can see statically; neither is a proof."
    ]
}

priority "truthful-over-convenient" {
    statement "A status that overstates is worse than one that blocks. Unevaluable is never GREEN, YELLOW is not success, and a false STALE is fine where a stale GREEN never is. When a clearer signal and an honest one disagree, the honest one wins."
}

priority "steering-cost-over-token-cost" {
    statement "Use a strong model where its reasoning creates real value, not on work an approved smaller model can safely do. Cheapest is not the goal: a delegation that comes back as review burden, an oversized diff, repeated questions or cleanup saved nothing. The steering and rework a change removes outrank the tokens it costs."
}

priority "bounded-workers-free-planners" {
    statement "A small worker makes bounded decisions inside its scope and reports a contradiction instead of silently redesigning. A strong planner is expected to challenge assumptions, name missing expertise and propose a larger change when the evidence supports it; a corrected direction is worth more than compliance. These are different jobs, and their guidance is never merged into one."
}

priority "disclosure-over-dumping" {
    statement "Project memory earns its place by what an agent can skip reading. Every surface answers at the coarsest identity that settles the question and gives detail only when asked. Replacing a large prompt with a large .bla dump is the failure this project exists to avoid."
}

priority "proportionate-verification" {
    statement "Verification makes ordinary development safe and is pointed at what changed. A check that makes ordinary development unreasonably slow has stopped paying for itself, whatever it proves."
}
